From 11033da436bbff2d5a39acffe6bd42be6058c747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 31 Mar 2026 23:39:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] fall back to sysfs touch poke when samsung sysinput HAL is
 missing

on samsung devices where the sysinput HIDL HAL
(vendor.samsung.hardware.sysinput@1.1) is not declared in the VINTF
manifest, the existing setTspEnable() call silently no-ops.  this
leaves the novatek (and other sec_input) touch controller stuck in
its suspended state after a display power cycle, permanently killing
touch input until reboot.

when the HAL lookup fails, fall back to writing 'check_connection'
to /sys/class/sec/tsp/cmd on display wake (STATE_ON).  this forces
the touch driver to re-establish communication with the touch IC,
which is the same mechanism used by standalone workarounds (magisk
modules) for exynos 850 GSI builds.

the sysfs node is guarded by an existence check and the write is
wrapped in a try/catch, so this is a no-op on non-samsung devices
or devices where the HAL works normally.

rw-system.sh already chowns /sys/class/sec/tsp/cmd to system and
relabels it to sysfs_ss_writable on samsung devices.
---
 .../server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java   | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
index 6865a23a7..3c4c68d6e 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
@@ -1004,6 +1004,30 @@ final class LocalDisplayAdapter extends DisplayAdapter {
                             }
                         }
 
+                        // fallback: when the samsung sysinput HAL is missing (not
+                        // declared in the device VINTF manifest), poke the touch
+                        // controller via sysfs to re-establish communication after
+                        // waking from suspend.  without this, touch input dies
+                        // permanently on exynos 850 and similar samsung SoCs.
+                        if (samsungSysinput == null
+                                && state == Display.STATE_ON
+                                && triedSamsungHal) {
+                            try {
+                                java.io.File tspCmd =
+                                        new java.io.File("/sys/class/sec/tsp/cmd");
+                                if (tspCmd.exists()) {
+                                    java.io.FileOutputStream fos =
+                                            new java.io.FileOutputStream(tspCmd);
+                                    fos.write("check_connection".getBytes());
+                                    fos.close();
+                                    Log.d("PHH", "Sent check_connection to "
+                                            + "sec/tsp/cmd (sysinput HAL unavailable)");
+                                }
+                            } catch (Throwable t) {
+                                Log.d("PHH", "Failed to poke sec/tsp/cmd", t);
+                            }
+                        }
+
                         setCommittedState(state);
 
                         // If we're entering a suspended (but not OFF) power state and we
